      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Implementation Steps**\n\nOkay, I'm zeroing in on the task: developing `stream_completion.py`. I've decided to move forward by making Google Cloud Vertex AI a concrete choice for the hosted LLM. This will be the first identifiable step in the code. I am also planning what the next steps will be.\n\n\n**Outlining Initial Implementation**\n\nI've got the initial steps for `stream_completion.py` mapped out. My focus is on making it a tangible implementation. I'm starting by establishing a function that streams output from the chosen hosted LLM, which is Vertex AI. I'll be using `google.cloud.aiplatform`, as this is a library for the model, which is likely `gemini-pro`. Making this clearly identifiable in the code is key.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820068612,
          "start": 1789820066971
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b996dc9b0014frLaKTr68lJ31",
